stem Instructions]\\n\" + \"\\n\".join(system_lines) + \"\\n\\n\" + last_user\n601:         if last_user:\n602:             return last_user\n603: \n604:     system_lines = []\n605:     dialogue_lines = []\n606: \n607:     for m in messages:\n608:         content = m.content or \"\"\n609:         if isinstance(content, list):\n610:             content = \" \".join([p.get(\"text\", \"\") for p in content if isinstance(p, dict) and \"text\" in p])\n611:         content = str(content).strip()\n612: \n613:         if m.role == \"system\":\n614:             system_lines.append(content)\n615:         elif m.role == \"user\":\n616:             dialogue_lines.append(f\"User: {content}\")\n617:         elif m.role == \"assistant\":\n618:             dialogue_lines.append(f\"Assistant: {content}\")\n619: \n620:     if len(dialogue_lines) == 1 and not system_lines:\n621:         return dialogue_lines[0].replace(\"User: \", \"\", 1)\n622: \n623:     parts = []\n624:     if system_lines:\n625:         parts.append(\"[System Instructions]\\n\" + \"\\n\".join(system_lines))\n626:     if dialogue_lines:\n627:         parts.append(\"\\n\".join(dialogue_lines))\n628: \n629:     return \"\\n\\n\".join(parts)\n630: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":6713,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-24T14:34:40Z","thinking":"The code aims to format a series of messages into a single prompt. If a flag is not set and there are existing messages, the code extracts the latest user input from the message history. This extraction is done by iterating in reverse order through the messages and identifying the first message from the user. It constructs the prompt by retrieving the user's content.\n\n\nThe current logic might inadvertently omit essential context. Specifically, the system instructions are only included if the message count is two or fewer. This conditional check suggests that with a history greater than two exchanges, the system instructions will be dropped. Consequently, the model will receive no guiding instructions. This omission can result in undesirable responses.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"Select-String -Path \"D:\\AI_Engineer\\MSEMAX-GAIStudio\\app.py\" -Pattern \"ensure_model|select.*model|model.*select\"","Cwd":"d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy","IsDaemon":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Search model selector in app.py","toolSummary":"Check if model selector exists in MSEMAX app.py"}}]}
